# No Deleting Documentation

Do not delete authored documentation during cleanup, refactors, or “tidying.”

That covers:

- `docs/handoffs/` and `docs/reference/`
- `docs/paper/` sources (`.tex`, `.bib`) and figures the manuscript uses
- `notebooks/` tutorials
- `README.md` and other markdown

Handoffs and reference notes stay after a fix lands. They are the record of why a convention or formula was chosen. When a note is obsolete, add a short superseded banner and point at the current code or the newer note.

Remove a doc only when the user asks to delete that file or names the paths to remove.

Generated TeX intermediates (`.aux`, `.log`, `.blg`, `.synctex.gz`, `.texpadtmp/`) are build products. Leave committed ones in place unless the user asks for them to be removed.
